00:01:14.418 --> 00:01:19.082
<v BREDA> Hello, Wayside Camera Club, Breda speaking.

00:01:19.083 --> 00:01:23.539
<v DAN> Oh, hello, um, my name's Dan and I'd like to join your club.

00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:32.519
<v BREDA> That's great, Dan. We have an application form – would you like to complete it over the phone, then you can ask any questions you might have?

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.722
<v DAN> Oh, yes, thanks.

00:01:33.723 --> 00:01:37.093
<v BREDA> OK, so what's your family name?

00:01:37.095 --> 00:01:39.445
<v DAN> It's Green – Dan Green.

00:01:39.446 --> 00:01:42.548
<v BREDA> So – can I take your email address?

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:49.954
<v DAN> Yes, it's dan1068@market.com.

00:01:49.955 --> 00:01:53.633
<v BREDA> Thanks. And what about your home address?

00:01:53.635 --> 00:02:00.816
<v DAN> Well, I'm about ten miles away from your club in Peacetown. I live in a house there.

00:02:00.818 --> 00:02:04.421
<v BREDA> OK, so what's the house number and street?

00:02:04.422 --> 00:02:08.308
<v DAN> It's 52 Marrowfield Street.

00:02:08.309 --> 00:02:19.637
<v BREDA> Is that M-A double R-O-W-F-I-E-L-D?

00:02:19.638 --> 00:02:20.756
<v DAN> That's right.

00:02:20.758 --> 00:02:23.540
<v BREDA> ...and that's Peacetown, you said?

00:02:23.541 --> 00:02:24.081
<v DAN> Uhuh.

00:02:24.082 --> 00:02:28.958
<v BREDA> So how did you hear about our club? Did you look on the internet?

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:37.577
<v DAN> I usually do that, but this time, well, I was talking to a relative the other day and he suggested it.

00:02:37.578 --> 00:02:39.710
<v BREDA> Oh, is he a member too?

00:02:39.712 --> 00:02:44.802
<v DAN> He belongs to another club – but he'd heard good things about yours.

00:02:44.802 --> 00:02:49.086
<v BREDA> OK. So what do you hope to get from joining?

00:02:49.087 --> 00:02:56.863
<v DAN> Well, one thing that really interests me is the competitions that you have. I enjoy entering those.

00:02:56.864 --> 00:02:59.025
<v BREDA> Right. Anything else?

00:02:59.027 --> 00:03:03.197
<v DAN> Well, I also like to socialise with other photographers.

00:03:03.198 --> 00:03:07.662
<v BREDA> That's great. So what type of membership would you like?

00:03:07.664 --> 00:03:09.196
<v DAN> What are the options?

00:03:09.198 --> 00:03:16.011
<v BREDA> It's £30 a year for full membership or £20 a year if you're an associate.

00:03:16.013 --> 00:03:19.609
<v DAN> I think I'll go for the full membership, then.

00:03:19.611 --> 00:03:25.762
<v BREDA> That's a good idea because you can't vote in meetings with an associate membership.

00:04:11.257 --> 00:04:15.165
<v BREDA> If I could just find out a bit more about you...

00:04:15.166 --> 00:04:15.980
<v DAN> OK.

00:04:15.981 --> 00:04:22.342
<v BREDA> So you said you wanted to compete – have you ever won any photography competitions?

00:04:22.343 --> 00:04:26.733
<v DAN> Not yet, but I have entered three in the past.

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:34.284
<v BREDA> Oh, that's interesting. So why don't you tell me something about those? Let's start with the first one.

00:04:34.285 --> 00:04:38.642
<v DAN> Well, the theme was entitled 'Domestic Life'.

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:43.197
<v BREDA> I see - so it had to be something related to the home?

00:04:43.198 --> 00:04:55.642
<v DAN> Yeah. I chose to take a photo of a family sitting round the dinner table having a meal, and, um, I didn't win, but I did get some feedback.

00:04:55.643 --> 00:04:58.113
<v BREDA> Oh, what did the judges say?

00:04:58.114 --> 00:05:00.874
<v DAN> That it was too 'busy' as a picture.

00:05:00.876 --> 00:05:06.462
<v BREDA> Aha – so it was the composition of the picture that they criticised?

00:05:06.463 --> 00:05:11.914
<v DAN> That's right – and once they'd told me that, I could see my mistake.

00:05:11.915 --> 00:05:15.360
<v BREDA> So what was the theme of the second competition?

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:24.618
<v DAN> Well, my university was on the coast and that area gets a lot of beautiful sunsets, so that was the theme.

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:28.249
<v BREDA> Oh, sunsets, that's a great theme.

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:36.647
<v DAN> Yes. The instructions were to capture the clouds as well – it couldn't just be blue sky and a setting sun.

00:05:36.649 --> 00:05:41.003
<v BREDA> Sure, cause they give you all those amazing pinks and purples.

00:05:41.004 --> 00:05:49.489
<v DAN> Yeah – and I thought I'd done that well, but the feedback was that I should have waited a bit longer to get the shot.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:52.998
<v BREDA> I see. So the timing wasn't right.

00:05:52.999 --> 00:06:01.694
<v DAN> Yes – I took it too soon, basically. And then the third competition I entered was called 'Animal Magic'.

00:06:01.695 --> 00:06:04.475
<v BREDA> Well, that's a difficult subject!

00:06:04.476 --> 00:06:08.329
<v DAN> I know! I had to take hundreds of shots.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:11.740
<v BREDA> I'm sure – because animals move all the time.

00:06:11.741 --> 00:06:28.721
<v DAN> That's what we had to show – there had to be some movement in the scene. I got a great shot of a fox in the end, but I took it at night and, well, I suspected that it was a bit dark, which is what I was told.

00:06:28.723 --> 00:06:39.231
<v BREDA> Well Dan – you seem to be really keen and we'd be delighted to have you in our club. I'm sure we can help with all those areas that you've outlined.

00:06:39.231 --> 00:06:40.871
<v DAN> Thanks, that's great.